{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ensembles runs alongside your app’s normal Core Data or SwiftData usage, and almost everything can happen at any time. This article covers the small set of rules that do matter: the one window in which saving causes problems, the signals that actually indicate sync success, and the recovery path for a device whose syncs keep failing.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"When-the-App-May-Save","text":"When the App May Save","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Saving is safe at almost any time. There is one window where a save causes real trouble, and one where it causes minor churn:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"During attach, a save aborts the attach","type":"text"}]},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleError\/saveOccurredDuringAttaching"},{"text":" (code 206). The partial state is discarded, so nothing is corrupted, but every retry re-imports the entire store. An app that saves constantly can keep aborting its own attach indefinitely.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"During a merge, a save aborts that merge","type":"text"}]},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleError\/saveOccurredDuringMerge"},{"text":" (code 207). The sync retries the merge a couple of times internally — the retry includes the new save’s event — and if the retries are exhausted, the merge simply reruns on the next sync trigger. This is routine in moderation; it only matters if the app saves so often that every merge window contains a save, in which case the device never completes a merge and quietly falls behind.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This reduces to one practical rule:","type":"text"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Hold writes until the first successful ","type":"text"},{"code":"sync()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" after launch. After that, save freely.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One pattern deserves a specific warning: ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"saving in response to merged changes","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". If a merge-notification handler (the containers’ ","type":"text"},{"code":"didSaveMergeChanges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the delegate’s equivalent, or an observer that rebuilds derived state when imported objects appear) performs a save, every merge that delivers data provokes a save, and that save aborts the next batch of the very merge that triggered it. The internal retry absorbs the occasional reactive save — the second pass delivers nothing new, so a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"purely","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" reactive app converges — but a handler that saves on every pass defeats it, and the device fails every sync while its store slowly fills from the committed batches. Prefer deferring reactive writes until the sync has completed: queue them, and flush when ","type":"text"},{"code":"sync()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns or on ","type":"text"},{"code":".coreDataEnsembleWillEndActivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The first successful sync proves attach is complete. Gating on that is more dependable than checking ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/currentActivity"},{"text":" before saving — a sync can begin between the check and the save, so an activity-based gate cannot be made race-free from outside the framework. Coalescing frequent writes into fewer saves remains good hygiene, because it shrinks the number of merge windows a save can land in, but it is an optimization, not a correctness requirement.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Detecting-Success-and-Staleness","text":"Detecting Success and Staleness","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/currentActivity"},{"text":" reports only what the ensemble is doing ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"right now","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":".none","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" means idle — it does not mean the last sync succeeded or that the device is up to date.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The reliable signals are tied to a specific sync:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The containers’ ","type":"text"},{"code":"sync()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when that sync completed, ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when it failed (the error goes to the container’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"didEncounterError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" callback).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/sync(options:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" throws on failure; returning normally means that sync succeeded.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":".coreDataEnsembleWillEndActivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" notification carries any error under ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleNotificationKey\/activityError","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To detect a stale device, record the time of each success and compare it against your auto-sync cadence:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["if await container.sync() {","    UserDefaults.standard.set(Date(), forKey: \"lastSuccessfulSync\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most sync errors are transient and clear on the next trigger. A device is in trouble only when the same error repeats across many attempts. Errors bridge to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSError"},{"type":"text","text":" with the domain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CDEErrorDomain"},{"type":"text","text":" and the case’s raw value as the code, and their descriptions name the case, so logs are self-diagnosing."}]},{"text":"Recovering a Stale Device","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Recovering-a-Stale-Device"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When one device fails every sync while the rest of the fleet is healthy:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Diagnose first."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Quiesce all writes, enable verbose logging with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setLoggingLevel(.verbose)"},{"text":", and run one manual sync. If it succeeds, the app was saving into every merge window — revisit the rule above. If it fails, the log names the real error.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Detach and re-attach."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Call the container’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"detach()"},{"text":", then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sync()"},{"text":". Local data is preserved and re-imported; the sync metadata is rebuilt from the cloud. This is the standard remedy.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rebuild from the cloud."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" If the device’s data is only a stale copy of what the cloud already holds, detach, delete the local store and local event data directory, recreate the stack, and sync. Unsynced local changes are lost, so reserve this for devices with nothing unique to keep."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Forcing a rebase ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions\/forceRebase","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") is not a recovery tool: it compacts event history, it does not repair a failing device."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a coordinated fresh start — for example, after duplicate identities accumulated because devices attached before global identifiers were configured — de-duplicate app-side on every device, detach all devices, remove the cloud data with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/removeEnsemble(withIdentifier:in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", wait for the deletion to propagate, then seed the cloud from your best device before bringing in the others."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncLifecycle"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/ConflictResolution","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleError"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/synclifecycle"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}],"role":"article","title":"Sync Lifecycle and Recovery","roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Know when the app may save, how to detect sync success and failure, and how to recover a device that has fallen behind."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles"]]},"references":{"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SyncOptions/forceRebase":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"forceRebase"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:9Ensembles11SyncOptionsV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SyncOptions"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/syncoptions\/forcerebase","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"forceRebase","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions\/forceRebase","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Force a rebase to compress sync data. More expensive but reduces storage."}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CoreDataEnsembleDelegate"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensembledelegate","title":"CoreDataEnsembleDelegate","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"CoreDataEnsembleDelegate","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Methods invoked by "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble"},{"type":"text","text":" to inform of sync-related changes."}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/EnsembleError/saveOccurredDuringMerge":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"saveOccurredDuringMerge"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/ensembleerror\/saveoccurredduringmerge","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"EnsembleError.saveOccurredDuringMerge","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleError\/saveOccurredDuringMerge","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A save occurred during a merge operation. The merge is aborted (after a few in-sync retries). Transient — retry the sync. If it recurs on every sync, look for app code that saves in response to merged changes, such as a merge-notification handler rebuilding derived state."}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/EnsembleError/saveOccurredDuringAttaching":{"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"saveOccurredDuringAttaching","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/ensembleerror\/saveoccurredduringattaching","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleError\/saveOccurredDuringAttaching","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A save occurred while the ensemble was attaching. The attach is aborted. Transient — retry attach after the save completes."}],"title":"EnsembleError.saveOccurredDuringAttaching"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/GettingStarted":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GettingStarted","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/gettingstarted","title":"Getting Started","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Set up Ensembles to sync a Core Data or SwiftData persistent store across devices."}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsemble/removeEnsemble(withIdentifier:in:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"removeEnsemble","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"withIdentifier","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"any","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CloudFileSystem","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:9Ensembles15CloudFileSystemP"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemble\/removeensemble(withidentifier:in:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/removeEnsemble(withIdentifier:in:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Completely removes the cloud data of an ensemble."}],"title":"removeEnsemble(withIdentifier:in:)"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/ConflictResolution":{"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/conflictresolution","kind":"article","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/ConflictResolution","abstract":[{"text":"Understand how Ensembles resolves conflicts and how to customize the process.","type":"text"}],"title":"Conflict Resolution"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsemble/sync(options:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sync","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"options","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:9Ensembles11SyncOptionsV","text":"SyncOptions","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemble\/sync(options:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/sync(options:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Syncs changes with other peers.","type":"text"}],"title":"sync(options:)"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Sync Core Data and SwiftData stores across devices using event sourcing.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles","type":"topic","title":"Ensembles","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsemble":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CoreDataEnsemble","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The central class of Ensembles, representing a set of synchronizing persistent stores.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemble","type":"topic","title":"CoreDataEnsemble","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CoreDataEnsemble","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/EnsembleError":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleError","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EnsembleError"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EnsembleError"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/ensembleerror","title":"EnsembleError"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsemble/currentActivity":{"title":"currentActivity","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemble\/currentactivity","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The activity currently being undertaken, if any."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"currentActivity"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EnsembleActivity","preciseIdentifier":"s:9Ensembles16EnsembleActivityO"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/currentActivity"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SwiftDataIntegration":{"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/swiftdataintegration","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"SwiftData Integration","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sync SwiftData models with Ensembles using "},{"code":"SwiftDataEnsembleContainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/EnsembleNotificationKey/activityError":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"activityError"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/ensemblenotificationkey\/activityerror","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/EnsembleNotificationKey\/activityError","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" present when an activity ends with a failure."}],"title":"activityError"},"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/CoreDataEnsembleContainer":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CoreDataEnsembleContainer","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ensembles\/coredataensemblecontainer","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CoreDataEnsembleContainer","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"CoreDataEnsembleContainer","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A high-level container that sets up a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","type":"reference"},{"text":" with automatic syncing,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delegate management, and optional Core Data stack creation.","type":"text"}]}}}